      "answer": "Quotient $2x^2-2x-4$; remainder $10x-15$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Divide to obtain a quotient of the form $2x^2\\pm2x+k$ ($k\\ne0$) — M1. Guidance: obtain the result together with a linear polynomial or a constant as remainder.\n\nObtain quotient $2x^2-2x-4$ — A1. Guidance: allow unless quotient and remainder are interchanged, then A0 A1.\n\nObtain remainder $10x-15$ — A1. Guidance: allow $(x^2+x+3)(2x^2-2x-4)+10x-15$.\n\nAlternative method: expand $(x^2+x+3)(Ax^2+Bx+C)+Dx+E$ and reach $A=2$, $B=\\pm2$, $C=k$ — M1. Guidance: solve all three equations for $A,B,C$; allow sign errors in establishing equations and in solving. If correct: $A=2$, $A+B=0$, $3A+B+C=0$, $3B+C+D=0$, $3C+E=-27$. Then obtain quotient $2x^2-2x-4$ — A1, and remainder $10x-15$ — A1, with the same interchange guidance.\n\nTotal: 3",
